        "by": "human",
        "reason": "Downstream SQL-on-FHIR consumers join derived tables on getResourceKey() resource keys, which the port computes internally but drops at the outermost SELECT. The attempt adds the paired key column beside each MIMIC identifier column (subject_id->patient_key, hadm_id->encounter_key, stay_id->icu_encounter_key, specimen_id->specimen_key). Additive and shape-only: both comparison paths project manifest columns explicitly, so no compared value can change. The MIMIC integer columns are retained as the oracle join keys.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "Phenylephrine attempt 0002 faithfully maps the exact ICU MedicationAdministration code, preserves all 193,260 source-event rows and multiplicity, and uses every available FHIR path. ICU ETL irreversibly casts start/end times through TIMESTAMPTZ (mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_medication_administration_icu.sql:8-9,61-69) and writes amount into six-decimal dosage.dose.value (:12,85-90), while omitting linkorderid and patientweight (:7-23,38-100). Rate unit survives in dosage.rateQuantity.unit (:91-98), so the one uncomputable mcg/min rate is correctly NULL rather than estimated. The reported residual conflicts are amplified by unkeyed stay-only pairing, not evidence of another mapping defect. These losses are intrinsic and ancillary: they do not change row inclusion, grain, grouping, carry-forward, or other clinically meaningful outputs.",
        "superseded_status": "COMPLETED_WITH_DIVERGENCE"
      }
    ],
